A||N||5||Kelvin Vivian||Horn Doesn't  Work||||4||
Z||000000||Kelvin Vivian||01-26-2001||03:27 AM||||The horn in the 88 usually doesn't work. However, one day, it worked!<P>I kind of wished I would have tested the power mirrors while my horn worked. But as of now, the horn is dead, and the power mirrors do not work. I've replaced the power mirror switch, still no go.<P>Any ideas of where I should get started?<P>Thanks<BR>Kelvin<BR>87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd <BR>88 GT, 5-spd <BR> <BR>||||reg||4
Z||000001||FieroJoe||01-26-2001||08:35 AM||||Do you have any other power options?  If they also do not work, check the fuse.  If you push the horn button and hear a clicking from underneath the passenger side dash, then you know you need to check the connections at the horns.  That clicking is the horn relay.  It is a little white box next to the hazard flasher relay and the blue chime box.  Their relative position make them easy to get kicked, so possibly it is loose, or just bad.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||01-26-2001||08:49 PM||||Those circuits are spread over multiple fuses. check all the fuses and the fuse links in the engine compartment If this is an 84 there are fuse links on the starter. all other years they are all by the battery as far as I know.<P>the horn relay is on the passengers side under the dash. small white square thing on the side of the heater housing. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rodmcneill||01-26-2001||10:12 PM||||I had a Grand Am that both horns went bad, first one, then the other one just croaked. Get a test light, disconnect the wire at the horn under the car, see if the test light works, if it does light then the horn has gone bad. Also check the wire and connector for corrosion. It could also be a relay or wiring. On electrical problems I like to start at one end and work my way back.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Kelvin Vivian||01-26-2001||11:21 PM||||Thanks for the tips...<P>The power door locks on the car work fine...<P>Once I figure out what's wrong, I'll post it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||01-26-2001||11:45 PM||||Make sure the horn is making a good ground to the body.||||reg||1
